change locate-line-index {
    summary "Locate spans through a line-start index"
    category performance
    impact public
    touches "pkg/rs/parse"
    commit "c87fe9c8722d71ea90e0505d37876ba8d39be7c9"
    detail "Resolving a span's line and column rescanned the document from a checkpoint for every span that lay before the previous one, and a binder locates each node's spans out of order, so locating cost time quadratic in a document's size and half of a reading's time. The locator now indexes the document's line starts once, on its first lookup; each later lookup is a binary search and a count over one line's prefix, and a lookup on the line of the one before it is the count alone."
}
